  "id": "Compound::DB01148 - Gene::5144",
  "verbalization": "Flavoxate is implicated in the regulation of 3',5'-cyclic-AMP phosphodiesterase activity through its interaction with Pde8b or Pde8a, which in turn are involved in the same enzymatic function as Pde4d. This suggests that Flavoxate may influence Pde4d through a shared pathway involving the regulation of cyclic AMP hydrolysis. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Flavoxate's binding to Pde8 family members leads to a functional role in phosphodiesterase activity, which is a common feature of Pde4d. The consistent involvement of Pde4d in this process, across different Pde8 isoforms, highlights a potential mechanism by which Flavoxate could modulate Pde4d activity. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Flavoxate exerts its effects on Pde4d through a mechanism involving the regulation of cyclic AMP hydrolysis, likely through the Pde8 family of enzymes.",
